      "notes": "<h2>Interjections</h2>\n<h3>1. UNDERSTANDING INTERJECTIONS</h3>\n<p>An <b>interjection</b> is a word or short phrase used to express sudden emotion, feeling, surprise, or exclamation. It usually stands outside the main grammatical structure of a sentence.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Joy/Delight:</b> Hurray! Wow! Yay!</li>\n<li><b>Pain/Discomfort:</b> Ouch! Ah! Oh!</li>\n<li><b>Surprise/Astonishment:</b> Gosh! Heavens! Oh no!</li>\n<li><b>Hesitation/Attention:</b> Um, er, hey, shh, look!</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. PUNCTUATION RULES</h3>\n<p>Use an <b>exclamation mark (!)</b> for strong emotions (<i>Ouch! That hurt.</i>) and a <b>comma (,)</b> for mild expressions (<i>Well, let us start.</i>).</p>",
