      "notes": "<h2>Reported Speech (Indirect Speech)</h2>\n<h3>1. WHAT IS REPORTED SPEECH?</h3>\n<p><b>Reported speech</b> reports what someone said without using their exact words and without quotation marks.</p>\n<h3>2. KEY TRANSFORMATION RULES (BACKSHIFTING)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Present Simple → Past Simple:</b> <i>“I like tea” → He said that he liked tea.</i></li>\n<li><b>Present Continuous → Past Continuous:</b> <i>“I am reading” → She said she was reading.</i></li>\n<li><b>Past Simple → Past Perfect:</b> <i>“I saw him” → He said he had seen him.</i></li>\n<li><b>Will → Would / Can → Could / May → Might</b></li>\n<li><b>Time & Place shifts:</b> now → then, today → that day, tomorrow → the next day, here → there.</li>\n</ul>",
