          "q": "Analyse the persuasive language in this statement: 'Will we wait until another riverbank collapses before protecting our homes? Plant grass and trees along the river today.' Identify the rhetorical question and the call to action, then explain their effects.",
          "ans": "The rhetorical question is 'Will we wait until another riverbank collapses before protecting our homes?' It highlights a possible danger and creates urgency. The call to action is 'Plant grass and trees along the river today.' It tells readers what action the writer wants them to take.",
